---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import {
  INACTIVITY_DAYS,
  LEGAL_UPDATED,
  NOT_AFFILIATED,
  OPERATOR_EMAIL,
  OPERATOR_NAME,
  TRAKT_CONNECTED_APPS_URL,
  TRAKT_PRIVACY_URL,
} from '../data/site';

const CNIL_URL = 'https://www.cnil.fr/';
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="Privacy policy of the hosted Trakt MCP service: what it stores about you, what it never stores (your viewing data), and how to erase your data."
  path="/privacy"
  updated={LEGAL_UPDATED}
>
  <h2>Who runs this service</h2>
  <p>
    This service is operated by {OPERATOR_NAME}, an individual, who is responsible for your data. Contact:{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR_EMAIL}`}>{OPERATOR_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>
  <p>{NOT_AFFILIATED}</p>

  <h2>What the service does</h2>
  <p>
    It lets an AI assistant you connect, such as Claude or ChatGPT, browse the Trakt catalog and read and update your
    Trakt account: watchlist, watch history, collection, ratings, check-ins and recommendations. Every tool call reads or
    writes Trakt directly; nothing about your viewing data is kept.
  </p>

  <h2>What is stored</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Your Trakt user id and your Trakt username slug, with the dates your account was created and last used. The slug
      lets the operator find your account when you ask to be disconnected.
    </li>
    <li>Your Trakt access and refresh tokens, encrypted, with the expiry of the access token.</li>
    <li>Hashes of the tokens this server issues to your assistant, with their expiry. Never the tokens themselves.</li>
    <li>The assistants (OAuth clients) registered with this server, or described by their own metadata document.</li>
    <li>Sign-ins in progress: they expire after 10 minutes and are deleted within the hour.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is never stored</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your watch history, watchlist, ratings and collection.</li>
    <li>Comments, and the tool inputs and outputs exchanged with your assistant.</li>
    <li>Any token in clear.</li>
    <li>Watch history, ratings, tool arguments or results in logs at the default log level.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    At the default log level, each tool call writes one log line: the tool name, an internal user id, the duration, the
    status, the Trakt HTTP status and the number of results. At that level, arguments and results are not logged, and
    tokens never are.
  </p>

  <h2>Use of Trakt data</h2>
  <p>
    Trakt is the data source and processor of your viewing data: your history, ratings, watchlist and collection live at
    Trakt, under <a href={TRAKT_PRIVACY_URL}>Trakt's own privacy policy</a>. This service reads and writes them on your
    behalf, only to perform the actions your assistant requests.
  </p>
  <p>
    The results of those actions are returned to the assistant you connected, and handled by its provider under its own
    privacy policy. This service does not share them with anyone else, sell them, or use them for advertising or to
    train models.
  </p>

  <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The tokens issued to your assistant expire after 1 hour (access) and 180 days without use (refresh).</li>
    <li>
      An account unused for {INACTIVITY_DAYS} days is purged automatically: its rows are deleted, then its Trakt grant is
      revoked.
    </li>
    <li>
      An assistant registered with the server is deleted when it has not been used for {INACTIVITY_DAYS} days, or 24 hours
      after registering if it never signed anyone in.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to erase everything</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Disconnect the connector in your assistant. A client that calls the revoke endpoint has its tokens revoked, so it
      can no longer act on your account. This does not delete your account row and does not revoke the application at
      Trakt.
    </li>
    <li>
      Revoke the application at Trakt, under Settings, <a href={TRAKT_CONNECTED_APPS_URL}>Connected Apps</a>. The data
      stored about you is deleted the next time your assistant calls a tool and Trakt refuses the call; if that never
      happens, the automatic purge removes it.
    </li>
    <li>
      Ask the operator at <a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR_EMAIL}`}>{OPERATOR_EMAIL}</a> to disconnect you: your Trakt grant
      is revoked and every row about you is deleted from the live database at once.
    </li>
    <li>Stop using it: accounts unused for {INACTIVITY_DAYS} days are purged.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    After a revoke at Trakt, our rows stay until your next call fails or the {INACTIVITY_DAYS}-day purge runs, so deletion
    can take up to {INACTIVITY_DAYS} days. Only the operator's disconnection and the purge delete at once.
  </p>
  <p>
    The database lives on a persistent storage volume. Deleted data can remain in backups of that volume, if the operator
    or the hosting provider keeps any, until they expire under the backup retention; Trakt tokens stay encrypted there
    too.
  </p>

  <h2>Legal basis and recipients</h2>
  <p>
    Your data is processed only to provide the service you asked for: connecting your assistant to your Trakt account.
  </p>
  <p>
    It is handled by Trakt, which holds your viewing data; by the assistant you connect; and by the hosting provider that
    stores this service's database.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask for a copy of the data stored about you, in a portable format, or for its correction, restriction or
    deletion, and you can object to its processing, by e-mail. Your viewing data itself is held by Trakt: use Trakt's own
    tools for it. If you think your data is mishandled, you can complain to the CNIL, the French data protection
    authority, at <a href={CNIL_URL}>cnil.fr</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    This website sets no cookies and runs no analytics. It loads nothing from another site: even its fonts are served from
    the site itself.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    When this policy changes, the date at the top changes too. The conditions of use are in the <a href="/terms"
      >terms of service</a
    >.
  </p>
</Legal>
